exists su name learning distillation prompt ob text quoted.text.You are distilling source material into a reusable educational teaching artifact.

Task:
Given SOURCE TEXT and LEARNING FOCUS, return one plain-text teaching block with these exact headings in this exact order:

SEED CONCEPT
CARDINAL TRAINING SENTENCE
ORTHOGONAL FEATURES
SURPRISES AND MISUNDERSTANDINGS
AFFAIRS OR ACTIVITIES
CAUSATIVE AND CONSEQUENCE
CARDINAL SCENES AND IDIOMS
BRIEF MEMORY PHRASES

Rules:
- Stay faithful to the source text.
- Use the learning focus as a lens, not a license to invent unsupported teaching.
- If the requested focus is only partly supported, stay with the nearest supported teaching lane.
- If the focus is absent, say so plainly inside the teaching block rather than hallucinating details.
- Prefer plain language and teaching clarity over decorative summary.
- Remove greetings, speaker labels, transcript clutter, and side tangents.
- Prefer concrete practices, causes, and results over vague inspiration.
- Prefer the source's own symbolic world over generic spiritual filler.
- Do not flatten the source into generic academic, managerial, sociological, dictionary, or textbook language.
- Preserve the source's actual ontology, symbolic world, and mode of causation when distilling the teaching.
- If the source speaks in terms like Creator, consciousness, light, seeking, service, polarity, free will, energy, or spirit, do not replace those with generic abstractions like resources, authority, compliance, leverage, enforcement, persuasion, or social control unless the source itself clearly does so.
- Prefer communal declarative phrasing that states what is true, practiced, or learned.
- Prefer we, our, shared, or neutral collective language when it fits the source.
- Avoid direct second-person instruction and bare imperative phrasing when a declarative teaching line will do.
- Prefer present-tense realis teaching statements over commands, promises, or hypotheticals.
- Each section should default to declarative teaching statements, not advice commands.
- When a practice is important, describe the practice as something we do, cultivate, or observe rather than telling the reader what to do.
- Keep affirmative definitional material and corrective contrast in separate lanes when the source allows it.
- Prefer SEED CONCEPT and CARDINAL TRAINING SENTENCE to say what the teaching is and how it works, not mainly what it is not.
- Put paradoxes, corrections, negation-heavy clarifications, and common misunderstandings mainly in SURPRISES AND MISUNDERSTANDINGS rather than loading them into SEED CONCEPT.
- When the source expresses a valid idea in contrastive form, prefer rewriting it into positive declarative form for SEED CONCEPT and CARDINAL TRAINING SENTENCE rather than carrying over wording like rather than, instead of, not this but that, or unlike.

Section rules:
- SEED CONCEPT: 1 short paragraph or 1-2 sentences. Prefer positive declarative explanation of the core idea, system, or reality named by the source. Focus on what it is, how it works, or what kind of truth it states. Avoid making this section mainly contrastive, corrective, or misunderstanding-driven when the source provides enough affirmative material. Rewrite contrast-shaped source material into positive declarative teaching whenever the meaning can stay faithful.
- SEED CONCEPT: do not collapse a spiritually, symbolically, or metaphysically specific teaching into a generic definition that could fit an unrelated textbook or management guide.
- CARDINAL TRAINING SENTENCE: exactly 1 sentence, clear enough for a 12 year old, and written as a declarative teaching sentence rather than a command. Prefer a short affirmative operating truth, not a negation-heavy warning or correction, unless the source gives no stronger declarative line. Prefer a positive teaching sentence over contrastive wording when the same meaning can be stated cleanly.
- CARDINAL TRAINING SENTENCE: keep the sentence native to the source's actual teaching world; do not rewrite it into generic institutional or behavioral advice that the source itself does not support.
- ORTHOGONAL FEATURES: 3-5 short lines.
- SURPRISES AND MISUNDERSTANDINGS: 2-5 short lines naming source-supported paradoxes, corrections, surprises, or common misunderstandings clarified by the source.
- AFFAIRS OR ACTIVITIES: 2-5 short lines describing practices in declarative communal or neutral phrasing.
- CAUSATIVE AND CONSEQUENCE: 2-5 short lines showing practice and result.
- CARDINAL SCENES AND IDIOMS: 2-6 short lines.
- BRIEF MEMORY PHRASES: 4-10 short lines, each 2-8 words, preferably short declarative refrain-like phrases rather than commands.

Formatting rules:
- Plain text only.
- Use the exact headings above.
- Put each list item on its own line beginning with "- ".
- No markdown beyond those simple heading lines and dash list items.
- No extra headings, no commentary before or after the block..text.quoted be text ya

exists su name learning merge prompt ob text quoted.text.You are merging multiple concept-card teaching artifacts into one consolidated educational teaching artifact.

Task:
Given CHUNK CARDS and LEARNING FOCUS, return one plain-text teaching block with these exact headings in this exact order:

SEED CONCEPT
CARDINAL TRAINING SENTENCE
ORTHOGONAL FEATURES
SURPRISES AND MISUNDERSTANDINGS
AFFAIRS OR ACTIVITIES
CAUSATIVE AND CONSEQUENCE
CARDINAL SCENES AND IDIOMS
BRIEF MEMORY PHRASES

Rules:
- Keep the same schema exactly.
- Merge duplicates and near-duplicates.
- Preserve distinct supported ideas rather than collapsing everything into one narrow summary.
- Prefer conceptual breadth across the chunk cards.
- Do not invent claims that are not supported by the chunk cards.
- This is a schema-preserving merge, not a generic summary.
- Prefer communal declarative phrasing over direct instruction.
- Keep affirmative definition concentrated in SEED CONCEPT and CARDINAL TRAINING SENTENCE when the cards support it.
- Move contrastive or corrective material toward SURPRISES AND MISUNDERSTANDINGS instead of letting it dominate the seed sections.
- Rewrite contrast-shaped seed wording into positive declarative form when the merged cards already support the same meaning.
- Do not merge toward the lowest-common-denominator summary if the cards share a more specific spiritual, symbolic, or metaphysical teaching world.

Formatting rules:
- Plain text only.
- Use the exact headings above.
- Put each list item on its own line beginning with "- ".
- No markdown beyond those simple heading lines and dash list items.
- No extra headings, no commentary before or after the block..text.quoted be text ya

exists su name learning refine prompt ob text quoted.text.You are refining a concept-card teaching artifact into its clearest canonical form.

Task:
Given DRAFT CARD and LEARNING FOCUS, return one plain-text teaching block with these exact headings in this exact order:

SEED CONCEPT
CARDINAL TRAINING SENTENCE
ORTHOGONAL FEATURES
SURPRISES AND MISUNDERSTANDINGS
AFFAIRS OR ACTIVITIES
CAUSATIVE AND CONSEQUENCE
CARDINAL SCENES AND IDIOMS
BRIEF MEMORY PHRASES

Rules:
- Keep the same schema exactly.
- Keep all distinct supported concepts unless they are true duplicates.
- Remove redundancy and near-duplicate wording.
- Improve clarity and sharpen wording without narrowing the conceptual breadth.
- Prefer communal declarative phrasing over direct instruction.
- Prefer brief memory phrases that feel declarative and reusable.
- Do not add new claims not already present in the draft card.
- Strengthen affirmative declarative wording in SEED CONCEPT and CARDINAL TRAINING SENTENCE when the draft already supports it.
- Move corrective, paradox, or misunderstanding-heavy wording toward SURPRISES AND MISUNDERSTANDINGS when the draft mixes those lanes together.
- Rewrite rather-than, instead-of, or not-this-but-that seed wording into positive declarative teaching when the draft already supports the same meaning.
- Do not refine the card into a more generic, secular, institutional, or textbook-sounding artifact than the draft already is.

Formatting rules:
- Plain text only.
- Use the exact headings above.
- Put each list item on its own line beginning with "- ".
- No markdown beyond those simple heading lines and dash list items.
- No extra headings, no commentary before or after the block..text.quoted be text ya

exists su name learning source support verify prompt ob text quoted.text.Verify whether TEACHING stays faithful to the source material in SOURCE.

GENERATOR INTENT:
- The output is a distilled teaching artifact, not a free summary.
- Concrete teachings, practices, consequences, and central images must remain supported by SOURCE.
- Clear wording and light paraphrase are allowed, but unsupported claims are not.
- Concise synthesis is allowed when it combines ideas that are already clearly present in SOURCE.

Evaluate only source-grounded teaching content:
- seed concept claims,
- training sentence claims,
- listed features,
- listed activities or practices,
- listed cause and consequence claims,
- listed central scenes or idioms when presented as source-central,
- memory phrases when they restate teaching.

Ignore harmless phrasing cleanup or plain-language compression if the teaching stays faithful.
Do not fail merely because the distillation:
- compresses several supported ideas into one sentence,
- uses plainer teaching wording than the source,
- restates a supported relation more directly,
- turns source-supported imagery into short memory phrases.

PASS if:
- the teaching block remains faithful to SOURCE,
- concrete teaching statements are supported,
- no clear major meaning drift occurs.

FAIL if:
- important teaching claims, practices, or consequences clearly lack support,
- unsupported central images or doctrines are clearly added,
- a source-specific spiritual, symbolic, or metaphysical teaching is flattened into generic institutional, academic, managerial, sociological, or dictionary-style language,
- source-native causation is replaced with generic abstractions like control, resources, enforcement, persuasion, compliance, leverage, or hierarchy without clear support,
- the requested focus clearly causes material distortion of the source.

Output rules:
- First output one short paragraph (1-2 sentences, max 70 words).
- Final line must be exactly PASS or FAIL.
- No bullets, no labels, no markdown.
- No text after the final verdict line..text.quoted be text ya

exists su name learning source support verdict prompt ob text quoted.text.Read the verifier analysis and output exactly one word: PASS or FAIL.

Rules:
- Return FAIL only when the analysis clearly says the teaching block adds important unsupported claims, important unsupported practices, important unsupported consequences, or clear material meaning drift.
- Otherwise return PASS.
- One word only.
- No labels, no explanation, no punctuation..text.quoted be text ya

exists su name learning source support verify mind be mind fromtext name learning source support verify prompt ya
exists su name learning source support verdict mind be mind fromtext name learning source support verdict prompt ya

su name learning source support from text source with text teaching to name text pass be ceremony def
  su name learning source support request begin stage ob text "SOURCE:\n" to name text learning source support request be text do
  ob text of from of this to name learning source support request be plus do
  ob text "\n\nTEACHING:\n" to name learning source support request be plus do
  ob text of with of this to name learning source support request be plus do
  su name learning source support write stage ob name text learning source support request for name learning source support verify mind to name text learning source support review by num 0 atmost num 520 be write do
  su name learning source support verdict stage ob name text learning source support review for name learning source support verdict mind to name text learning source support pass be write do
  su name learning source support return stage ob name text learning source support pass be text do
prah

su name learn extract card from text source with text learning focus to name text teaching out be ceremony def
  su name learn source stage ob text of from of this to name text learn source text be text do
  su name learn focus stage ob text of with of this to name text learn focus text be text do
  ob name text learn focus text be equally from text "" then
  ob bool lie fromtext text "learning focus defective: give a non-empty learning focus" be guarantee do

  su name learning request begin stage ob text "LEARNING FOCUS:\n" to name text learning request be text do
  ob name text learn focus text to name learning request be plus do
  ob text "\n\nSOURCE TEXT:\n" to name learning request be plus do
  ob name text learn source text to name learning request be plus do

  su name teaching raw stage ob name text learning request fromtext name learning distillation prompt for name mind to name text teaching raw by num 0 atmost num 1400 be write do
  ob text "node command/extract_learn_pipeline_result.mjs" fromtext name teaching raw to name text teaching out be command do
  ob text "node command/normalize_learn_card.mjs" fromtext name teaching out to name text teaching out be command do
  ob text "node command/validate_learn_card.mjs" fromtext name teaching out to name text learning card valid be command do
  su name learning source support verify stage from text of ob of learn source text with text of ob of teaching out to name text learning source support pass be learning source support do
  ob text of ob of learning source support pass be equally from text "FAIL" then
  ob bool lie fromtext text "learning source support defective" be guarantee do
  su name teaching out ret
prah

su name learn merge cards from text cards with text learning focus to name text teaching out be ceremony def
  su name learn cards stage ob text of from of this to name text learn cards text be text do
  su name learn focus stage ob text of with of this to name text learn focus text be text do
  ob name text learn focus text be equally from text "" then
  ob bool lie fromtext text "learning focus defective: give a non-empty learning focus" be guarantee do

  su name learning merge request begin stage ob text "LEARNING FOCUS:\n" to name text learning merge request be text do
  ob name text learn focus text to name learning merge request be plus do
  ob text "\n\nCHUNK CARDS:\n" to name learning merge request be plus do
  ob name text learn cards text to name learning merge request be plus do

  su name teaching raw stage ob name text learning merge request fromtext name learning merge prompt for name mind to name text teaching raw by num 0 atmost num 2600 be write do
  ob text "node command/extract_learn_pipeline_result.mjs" fromtext name teaching raw to name text teaching out be command do
  ob text "node command/normalize_learn_card.mjs" fromtext name teaching out to name text teaching out be command do
  ob text "node command/validate_learn_card.mjs" fromtext name teaching out to name text learning card valid be command do
  su name teaching out ret
prah

su name learn refine card from text card with text learning focus to name text teaching out be ceremony def
  su name learn card stage ob text of from of this to name text learn card text be text do
  su name learn focus stage ob text of with of this to name text learn focus text be text do
  ob name text learn focus text be equally from text "" then
  ob bool lie fromtext text "learning focus defective: give a non-empty learning focus" be guarantee do

  su name learning refine request begin stage ob text "LEARNING FOCUS:\n" to name text learning refine request be text do
  ob name text learn focus text to name learning refine request be plus do
  ob text "\n\nDRAFT CARD:\n" to name learning refine request be plus do
